    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489-a1">

                <pb facs="0944" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg820"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Fernandez to
                        Señor Navarro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Secretaryship of State and Office of Foreign
                                Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 9, 1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>It having been shown by experience lasting for half a century, so far as this
                    country is concerned, that it is expedient to introduce certain modifications in
                    the treaties of navigation and commerce concluded by Mexico which should be in
                    harmony with <pb facs="0945" n="821" xml:id="pg821"/> the interests of both the
                    contracting parties, the President, resting on the stipulations contained in the
                    first paragraph of the thirty-fourth article of the treaty of April 5, 1831, and
                    in the seventeenth article of the treaty of February 2, 1848, both concluded
                    with the United States of America, has ordered that there be denounced to the
                    Government of Washington, as I now formally do through the medium of your
                    legation, the aforesaid treaty of navigation and commerce of April 5, 1831, as
                    annulled and not subsisting after the lapse of one year counting from the day
                    whereon your legation shall make the corresponding notification to the
                    Department of State, to which end you may inclose the present dispatch with your
                    note or annex thereto a copy hereof.</p>
                <p>I protest to you my particular esteem.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSÉ FERNANDEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
